; Run 3 on OPS-SAT PRETTY (exp4051), segment 3: the shrinking quorum with the
; manager's state file. One fault puts state into the file that must survive
; a kill:
;   cycle 200  replica 1 returns the same wrong value: outvoted on cycles
;              200, 201 and 202, fails its known-answer test and is retired
; The state file is saved on every change and, set here by command, every
; 100 cycles (the model's default is 1,000), so a kill loses at most 100.
; The entry script then kills the process without warning (SIGKILL) and
; starts it again with no sequence: the manager restores the policy, the
; slots (replica 1 retired) and the cycle counter from the file.
R00:00:00 MruOpsSat.manager.SET_POLICY SHRINK
R00:00:00 MruOpsSat.manager.STATESAVEPERIOD_PRM_SET 100
R00:00:00 MruOpsSat.injector.SET_UPSETS 0.0 0.05 1
R00:00:00 MruOpsSat.injector.INJECT STUCK 1 200
